### Description

<!--
What's the problem? How are we addressing it?

Write for a reviewer who has not worked in this part of the codebase. Give them the
background they need before the problem makes sense, and avoid jargon.
-->

Deleting a private repository also deletes all of its forks
([docs](https://docs.github.com/en/repositories/creating-and-managing-repositories/deleting-a-repository)). The web UI
warns about this before you confirm: "This will also delete all 3 forks since this is a private repository." Our [`repo
delete`
command](https://github.com/cli/cli/blob/f7a06a18a91eef5c0b218b549dab64b86f36f8b9/pkg/cmd/repo/delete/delete.go#L118-L12
4) doesn't. It only asks you to type the repo name, and `--yes` skips even that.

The person deleting often can't see those forks. Private forks only inherit team access from their upstream, not
individual access ([docs](https://docs.github.com/en/pull-requests/reference/forks#permissions-of-forks)).

`gh repo delete` now [looks up the
repo](https://github.com/cli/cli/blob/4948470b5a97a7fd839df5389527f575070ab2f8/pkg/cmd/repo/delete/http.go#L12-L44)
before deleting it. The [new
check](https://github.com/cli/cli/blob/4948470b5a97a7fd839df5389527f575070ab2f8/pkg/cmd/repo/delete/delete.go#L162-L199)
only steps in when the repo takes its forks with it:

```go
// A public repo keeps its forks, and deleting a fork leaves that fork's own forks alone
if !info.Private || info.Fork || info.ForksCount == 0 {
return nil
}
```

When it does step in:

- In a terminal, `gh` shows the same warning as the web UI, then asks `Delete OWNER/REPO and its forks?`, defaulting to
No. It asks even with `--yes`.
- Without a terminal, `gh` exits 1 unless you also pass the new `--accept-cascading-deletion-of-private-forks` flag.

